{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3_traceRadical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3_traceRadical","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L339-L354","doc":"**The weighted trace on `TL₃(δ)` has zero radical.**\n\nThis is the `⊇` half of `HeckeToTemperleyLieb`'s open item, at `n = 3`, with no\nhypothesis left standing in for semisimplicity: the decomposition is\n`tl3AlgEquiv`, and the weights are only required to be non-zero-divisors — which\n`TemperleyLiebTower.yw_pos` already gives for the Markov weights at `1 < q`.\n\nIt is `n = 3` only. Nothing here bears on general `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.prodTrace_traceRadical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.prodTrace_traceRadical","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L312-L337","doc":"The weighted trace has zero radical as soon as both weights are\nnon-zero-divisors. Unlike the general statement in\n`TraceRadicalNondegenerate`, this needs no field: the two blocks are concrete,\nso `Matrix.ext_iff_trace_mul_right` applies directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.prodTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.prodTrace","kind":"def","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L306-L310","doc":"A weighted trace on the decomposed algebra: `y₁` on the scalar block, `y₂`\non the `2 × 2` block. This is the shape `TraceRadicalNondegenerate` treats in\ngeneral — a weighted sum of block traces, which is what a Markov trace is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3AlgEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3AlgEquiv","kind":"def","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L289-L298","doc":"**`TL₃(δ) ≃ₐ[R] Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R × R` when `δ` and `δ² − 1` are\nunits** — the Wedderburn decomposition at `n = 3`.\n\nThe block shape `1 ⊕ 2` matches `TemperleyLiebTower.catalan_three`, which\nrecords the same decomposition as the partition count `1² + 2² = 5`, arrived at\nfrom the representation-theoretic side. The two now agree as theorems rather\nthan as a table and a table. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Rep5_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Rep5_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L281-L287","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Rep5_eq_linEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Rep5_eq_linEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L270-L279","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3LinEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3LinEquiv","kind":"def","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L266-L268","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Rep5_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Rep5_basis","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L259-L264","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3ImgBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3ImgBasis","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L254-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Img_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Img_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L229-L252","doc":"The images are independent. This is the content already inside\n`TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3_linearIndependent`; stated here in the target, where\n`Module.Basis.mk` can use it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Img_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Img_span","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L217-L227","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Img_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Img_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L193-L215","doc":"**Every element of `Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R × R` is this combination of the\nfive images.** The coefficients are the entries of the inverse of the `5 × 5`\nmatrix of images, which is why they are polynomial in `c` and `w` and why the\nstatement is an identity rather than an existence claim — inverting a matrix\nwhose determinant is `(δ² − 1)²` needs `w`, and nothing else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Img","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl3Img","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L186-L191","doc":"The five images of `tl3Rep5` on the basis `{1, e₀, e₁, e₀e₁, e₁e₀}`. The\nlast two are `tl3M₀_mul_tl3M₁` and `tl3M₁_mul_tl3M₀`, already computed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2AlgEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2AlgEquiv","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L165-L178","doc":"**`TL₂(δ) ≃ₐ[R] R × R` when `δ` is a unit.**\n\n`TemperleyLiebAlgebra` says of exactly this statement that it is *not* claimed\nthere, and gives the reason: it had no upper bound. `tl2Basis` supplied the\nupper bound; the remaining content is that `{(1,1), (δ,0)}` spans, whose\nobstruction is the determinant `−δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2Rep_eq_linEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2Rep_eq_linEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L153-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2LinEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2LinEquiv","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L149-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2Rep_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2Rep_basis","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L143-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2ImgBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2ImgBasis","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L140-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2Img_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2Img_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L122-L138","doc":"The images are independent: the second coordinate kills `g₀` on its own,\nand `δ` being a unit then kills `g₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2Img_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2Img_span","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L105-L120","doc":"`{(1,1), (δ,0)}` spans `R × R` as soon as `δ` is a unit — the `n = 2`\nsurjectivity computation, in the concrete target where it is one line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2Img","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.tl2Img","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L102-L103","doc":"The two images of `tl2Rep` on the basis `{1, e₀}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.nonZeroDivisor_of_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWedderburn.nonZeroDivisor_of_unit","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWedderburn.lean#L92-L96","signatureChunk":0}]}